he remaining outcomes. The most informative next analyses are the already registered interactions and remaining main effects: KRAS by TP53-loss interaction (H13), EGFR amplicon restriction in TP53-loss-negative cells (H14), SMARCA2 context interactions (H15 and newly registered TP53-loss and subtype interactions), remaining driver effects on KIF18A, RIT1, STAT3, and TMED10 (H17 to H20), expression-stratified MYC effects on RPL11 (H21), and the newly registered USP7 interaction by MYC amplification. If any of these reveal a consistent at-least-10% relative effect with adequate cells, that claim deserves validation; otherwise, further exploration should be curtailed in favor of the strongest replicated dataset-specific signals.",
  "research_notes": "Updated after validation. Supported dataset-specific associations: H5 SMARCA4 loss -> stronger SMARCA2 dependency; H6 MSI-high -> stronger WRN dependency; H8 TP53 loss -> weaker USP7 dependency; H16 KEAP1 loss -> weaker NFE2L2 dependency. These are accepted as associations in this dataset only, not causal or broadly generalizable claims. Rejected/no support: H2, H3 after validation, H4, H7, H9 original direction, H10, H11 direct, H12. H3 was the only validated main effect and failed to replicate a meaningful effect; close it, but keep H14 active as a separate context restriction. Active unresolved priorities: H1, H13, H14, H15, H17 to H21, plus newly registered H22-H24 context interactions for SMARCA2 and USP7. Validation status: one validation used and failed for H3; nine voluntary validation requests remain, but reserve them for clear context-specific or remaining-outcome discoveries rather than borderline main effects. Continue checking cell counts before rare subgroup or interaction analyses, use research markers D/E/F only as negative controls if needed, and avoid interpreting large dataset associations as mechanisms or generalizable biology."
